# Trends.md Source Summary

## Overview
Trends is introduced as a universal mental model for understanding patterns and relationships in complex situations. It serves as a conceptual tool for navigating complexity through pattern recognition.

## Cross-Source Perspectives
- Donella H. Meadows (*Limits to Growth*) — systems dynamics, feedback loops, resource and population trends
- Scott Galloway (*The Four*) — platform dominance, market concentration, tech titan macro-trends

## Key Concepts
- Trends as a mental shortcut for complexity
- Systemic trends (Meadows) vs. market trends (Galloway)
- Universal applicability across domains

